<translate>
<!--T:1-->
Used to define a model properties so it can be used in other elements of the game, most notably in {{ll|item (scripts)|item}} and {{ll|vehicle (scripts)|vehicle}}. The basic structure of a model block is as follows:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = cpp
| code = 
module YourModule {
  model YourModel {
    mesh = your_model,
    texture = your_model_texture,
  }
}
}}

<translate>
<!--T:2-->
{{ll|attachment (scripts)|attachment}} blocks can also be added to the model definition to specify how the model should be placed, rotated and scaled when attached to a parent model.

== Parameters == <!--T:3-->

<!--T:4-->
You can find a full list of the parameters in the
</translate> <translate><!--T:5--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/scripts/model.html ScriptsDocs]</translate><translate>
<!--T:6-->
.

== Example == <!--T:7-->
</translate>

{{CodeSnip
| lang = Java
| code =
model Burger
{
	mesh = Burger,
    scale = 1.5,
    static = true,
    texture = BurgerTex,

	attachment Bip01_Prop2
	{
		offset = 0.0142 0.0401 0.0000,
		rotate = -23.3606 21.2788 37.5386,
		scale = 0.8280,
	}
}
}}

